 ### Uncompressed NIfTI Byte-Range Streaming
-Streaming 3D volume data via HTTP byte-range requests without downloading the full file, optimized for specific access patterns [S2]. Request contiguous byte ranges corresponding to image planes based on volume dimensions (nx, ny, nz) and bytes per voxel (bpv) [S2]. Axial (k) slice cost: one contiguous range of `nx * ny * bpv` bytes. Coronal (j) plane cost: `nz` ranges of `nx * bpv` each. Sagittal (i) plane cost: `ny * nz` ranges of `bytesPerVoxel` each [S2]. Sagittal access requires `ny * nz` separate range requests, which is impractical due to server multipart range count caps. Reduced-resolution volumes cannot be fetched via byte ranges without reading the entire file [S2].
